1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,334
Administrator: help someone sign in again.

2
00:00:03,334 --> 00:00:08,246
Unlock an account, reset a lost
authenticator, and require a private

3
00:00:08,246 --> 00:00:12,113
password after confirming
the person's identity.

4
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:18,605
Use your agency's identity-verification
procedure before changing sign-in

5
00:00:18,605 --> 00:00:19,605
security.

6
00:00:19,605 --> 00:00:24,904
Confirm the person through a trusted
channel, not a message containing a code.

7
00:00:25,205 --> 00:00:29,334
Administrator accounts use an
authenticator or recovery code.

8
00:00:29,334 --> 00:00:33,524
Email verification is never
available to administrators.

9
00:00:33,887 --> 00:00:35,875
Open Administration, then Users.

10
00:00:35,875 --> 00:00:40,223
Filter by the person's name or user
name and open the correct account.

11
00:00:40,223 --> 00:00:43,791
You can manage only accounts
within your authority.

12
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:48,660
For a locked account, choose Unlock
account after verifying the person.

13
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:53,698
This clears the lock; it does not
change their password or authenticator.

14
00:00:54,056 --> 00:00:58,873
For a lost authenticator, choose
Reset MFA after verifying the person.

15
00:00:58,873 --> 00:01:04,708
The confirmation explains that active
sessions and old codes will stop working.

16
00:01:05,071 --> 00:01:08,815
Tell the person to sign in
again with their password,

17
00:01:08,815 --> 00:01:14,231
add the new MERIT authenticator entry,
and save the new recovery codes.

18
00:01:14,598 --> 00:01:19,968
If a password reset is also needed, enter
a new temporary password and select Ask

19
00:01:19,968 --> 00:01:23,816
them to choose a new password
at their next sign-in.

20
00:01:24,177 --> 00:01:25,365
Save the account.

21
00:01:25,365 --> 00:01:30,325
Share the temporary password only
through your approved secure channel.

22
00:01:30,325 --> 00:01:34,847
Never request the person's
authenticator or recovery codes.

23
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:39,417
The person completes MFA and
chooses a password only they know.

24
00:01:39,417 --> 00:01:45,307
If both password and authenticator were
lost, they must complete both reset paths.

25
00:01:45,669 --> 00:01:50,065
Another administrator must help an
administrator who cannot sign in.

26
00:01:50,065 --> 00:01:55,056
A platform administrator should
contact another platform administrator.

27
00:01:56,219 --> 00:02:00,104
In this video you verified
the account and unlocked it,

28
00:02:00,104 --> 00:02:05,614
reset MFA and explained re-enrollment,
and required a private password after a

29
00:02:05,614 --> 00:02:07,144
temporary reset.
